=== METRICS ===
TAR: fraction genuine verification scores >= threshold
FAR_human: fraction human impostor scores >= threshold
FAR_attack: fraction synthetic scores >= threshold
EER threshold: operating point where FPR ≈ FNR (used for PE decisions)
summarize_with_ci: mean, std, 95% CI (t-interval if n>=10 else bootstrap)
paired_far_test: Wilcoxon signed-rank (alternative greater); fallback paired t
Hypothesis claim printed: Attack FAR > human FAR (Wilcoxon p=…)

=== CURRENT_RESULTS ===
Source: latest FULL cohort run (mode=full, n_subjects=51, all CMU subjects,
feature_set=hold_flight, split_mode=fixed, enroll {1,2,3,4} verify {5},
classifier=svm ONLY, attacks=vae+gan, seed=42, tune_hyperparameters=true,
VAE epochs=200, GAN epochs=300, run_id=full_42_20260827T042239Z).
Artifacts: results/human_baseline.csv, attack_summary.csv,
statistical_summary.csv, hypothesis_tests.csv, run_meta.json, figures/*.png

Human baseline — SVM, mean across 51 subjects:
  TAR ≈ 0.953  (95% CI ≈ 0.940–0.965)
  FAR_human ≈ 0.046  (95% CI ≈ 0.033–0.058)
  EER ≈ 0.007 (mean)

Attack FAR — at same EER threshold, mean across 51 subjects:
  VAE/SVM ≈ 0.996  (95% CI ≈ 0.994–0.999)
  GAN/SVM ≈ 0.976  (95% CI ≈ 0.963–0.988)
  TAR (genuine) stays ≈ 0.953

Hypothesis tests (Wilcoxon signed-rank, H1: attack FAR > human FAR), n=51:
  VAE/SVM: ΔFAR=0.9505 ; p=2.572e-10
  GAN/SVM: ΔFAR=0.9299 ; p=2.572e-10

Conclusion (empirical, full cohort):
  RESEARCH_ANSWER: PE cannot reliably reject VAE/GAN impersonation.
  Human FAR ~4.6% vs attack FAR ~99.6% (VAE) / ~97.6% (GAN).
  Trust paradox strongly supported; VAE slightly more effective than GAN.

Earlier pilot (n=5, svm+rf, --no-tune) showed same direction with p≈0.03;
full cohort tightens CIs and yields much stronger significance.

Optional extensions not in this primary run:
  Random Forest classifier, LOSO (--split-mode losso), ablations (run_ablation.py)

